# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit26核心词汇

{{accommodate}}{{/əˈkɒmədeɪt}}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accumulate}}{{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt}}{{v. 积累；积聚}}{{Dust had accumulated on the shelves over the months.}}
{{ambiguous}}{{/æmˈbɪɡjuəs}}{{adj. 模棱两可的；含糊的}}{{The instructions were ambiguous and confusing.}}
{{anticipate}}{{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 预期；期望}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in demand.}}
{{applicable}}{{/əˈplɪkəbl}}{{adj. 适用的；可应用的}}{{The rule is applicable to all employees.}}
{{arbitrary}}{{/ˈɑːbɪtrəri}}{{adj. 任意的；武断的}}{{The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.}}
{{articulate}}{{/ɑːˈtɪkjuleɪt}}{{adj./v. 善于表达的；清楚表达}}{{She is very articulate and persuasive in debates.}}
{{assert}}{{/əˈsɜːt}}{{v. 断言；主张；维护}}{{She asserted her right to speak at the meeting.}}
{{attribute}}{{/əˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v./n. 归因于；属性}}{{She attributed her success to hard work.}}
{{authentic}}{{/ɔːˈθentɪk}}{{adj. 真正的；真实的}}{{The restaurant serves authentic Italian food.}}
{{authorize}}{{/ˈɔːθəraɪz}}{{v. 授权；批准}}{{The manager authorized the purchase of new equipment.}}
{{bias}}{{/ˈbaɪəs}}{{n./v. 偏见；偏向}}{{The report was criticized for its political bias.}}
{{catastrophe}}{{/kəˈtæstrəfi}}{{n. 灾难；大祸}}{{The oil spill was an environmental catastrophe.}}
{{chronic}}{{/ˈkrɒnɪk}}{{adj. 慢性的；长期的}}{{He suffers from chronic back pain.}}
{{conceive}}{{/kənˈsiːv}}{{v. 构想；怀孕；认为}}{{She conceived a plan to improve efficiency.}}
{{consensus}}{{/kənˈsensəs}}{{n. 共识；一致}}{{The committee reached a consensus on the new policy.}}
{{constitute}}{{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt}}{{v. 构成；组成}}{{Women constitute more than half of the population.}}
{{contemporary}}{{/kənˈtemprəri}}{{adj./n. 当代的；同时代的人}}{{The museum has a fine collection of contemporary art.}}
{{controversial}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl}}{{adj. 有争议的}}{{The new law is highly controversial among citizens.}}
{{convention}}{{/kənˈvenʃn}}{{n. 大会；惯例；公约}}{{The annual convention will be held in Shanghai.}}
{{cooperate}}{{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 合作；配合}}{{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.}}
{{correspond}}{{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 通信；相当于；符合}}{{The data does not correspond with the previous results.}}
{{deficit}}{{/ˈdefɪsɪt}}{{n. 赤字；不足；亏损}}{{The government is trying to reduce the budget deficit.}}
{{depict}}{{/dɪˈpɪkt}}{{v. 描绘；描述}}{{The painting depicts a beautiful landscape.}}
{{disclose}}{{/dɪsˈkləʊz}}{{v. 揭露；透露}}{{The company refused to disclose its financial information.}}
{{dispose}}{{/dɪsˈpəʊz}}{{v. 处理；布置；使倾向于}}{{Please dispose of the waste properly.}}
{{dramatic}}{{/drəˈmætɪk}}{{adj. 戏剧性的；巨大的}}{{There has been a dramatic change in the weather.}}
{{elaborate}}{{/ɪˈlæbərət}}{{adj./v. 精心制作的；详细阐述}}{{Could you elaborate on your proposal?}}
{{emit}}{{/ɪˈmɪt}}{{v. 发出；排放}}{{The factory emits large amounts of carbon dioxide.}}
{{enforce}}{{/ɪnˈfɔːs}}{{v. 执行；强制}}{{The police enforce the law to maintain order.}}
{{enterprise}}{{/ˈentəpraɪz}}{{n. 企业；事业}}{{The enterprise has grown into a multinational corporation.}}
{{entitle}}{{/ɪnˈtaɪtl}}{{v. 给予权利；给…命名}}{{This ticket entitles you to a free meal.}}
{{equivalent}}{{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt}}{{adj./n. 等同的；等价物}}{{One mile is equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.}}
{{evolve}}{{/ɪˈvɒlv}}{{v. 进化；发展}}{{Languages evolve over time.}}
{{exceed}}{{/ɪkˈsiːd}}{{v. 超过；超越}}{{Sales exceeded expectations this quarter.}}
{{exclude}}{{/ɪkˈskluːd}}{{v. 排除；排斥}}{{The price excludes tax and delivery charges.}}
{{execute}}{{/ˈeksɪkjuːt}}{{v. 执行；处决}}{{The plan was executed perfectly.}}
{{exploit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔɪt}}{{v./n. 开发；利用；功绩}}{{We should exploit renewable energy resources.}}
{{explicit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt}}{{adj. 明确的；清楚的}}{{The instructions must be explicit and easy to follow.}}
{{external}}{{/ɪkˈstɜːnl}}{{adj. 外部的；外面的}}{{The external walls of the building need repainting.}}
{{facilitate}}{{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt}}{{v. 促进；使便利}}{{Technology facilitates communication between people.}}
{{federal}}{{/ˈfedərəl}}{{adj. 联邦的}}{{The federal government passed a new tax law.}}
{{flourish}}{{/ˈflʌrɪʃ}}{{v. 繁荣；茂盛}}{{The business has flourished under new management.}}
{{formal}}{{/ˈfɔːml}}{{adj. 正式的；正规的}}{{The invitation requires formal attire.}}
{{foundation}}{{/faʊnˈdeɪʃn}}{{n. 基础；基金会}}{{Education is the foundation of a successful career.}}
{{framework}}{{/ˈfreɪmwɜːk}}{{n. 框架；结构}}{{The government established a new legal framework.}}
{{fraud}}{{/frɔːd}}{{n. 欺诈；骗子}}{{He was convicted of financial fraud.}}
{{fulfil/fulfill}}{{/fʊlˈfɪl}}{{v. 履行；实现；满足}}{{She fulfilled her dream of becoming a doctor.}}
{{fundamental}}{{/ˌfʌndəˈmentl}}{{adj. 基本的；根本的}}{{Freedom of speech is a fundamental human right.}}
{{generate}}{{/ˈdʒenəreɪt}}{{v. 产生；引起}}{{The wind turbines generate electricity for the town.}}
{{global}}{{/ˈɡləʊbl}}{{adj. 全球的；全面的}}{{Global warming is a major environmental concern.}}
{{govern}}{{/ˈɡʌvn}}{{v. 统治；管理；支配}}{{The country is governed by a democratic system.}}
{{guarantee}}{{/ˌɡærənˈtiː}}{{v./n. 保证；担保}}{{The product comes with a two-year guarantee.}}
{{identical}}{{/aɪˈdentɪkl}}{{adj. 完全相同的}}{{The two paintings look almost identical.}}
{{implement}}{{/ˈɪmplɪment}}{{v./n. 实施；工具}}{{The government plans to implement the new policy next year.}}
{{implication}}{{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn}}{{n. 含义；暗示；影响}}{{The findings have important implications for future research.}}
{{impose}}{{/ɪmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 强加；征收}}{{The government imposed a tax on luxury goods.}}
{{incline}}{{/ɪnˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 倾向；斜面}}{{I am inclined to agree with your suggestion.}}
{{inevitable}}{{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl}}{{adj. 不可避免的；必然的}}{{Change is inevitable in a rapidly developing world.}}
{{infer}}{{/ɪnˈfɜːr}}{{v. 推断；推论}}{{We can infer from the data that sales are improving.}}
{{inflation}}{{/ɪnˈfleɪʃn}}{{n. 通货膨胀；膨胀}}{{High inflation reduces the purchasing power of consumers.}}
{{ingredient}}{{/ɪnˈɡriːdiənt}}{{n. 成分；原料}}{{Fresh ingredients make the food taste better.}}
{{initiative}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv}}{{n. 主动性；倡议}}{{She took the initiative to organize the event.}}
{{innovation}}{{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn}}{{n. 创新；革新}}{{Innovation is the key to business success.}}
{{instinct}}{{/ˈɪnstɪŋkt}}{{n. 本能；直觉}}{{Animals rely on instinct to find food.}}
{{institution}}{{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn}}{{n. 机构；制度}}{{Universities are important educational institutions.}}
{{intellectual}}{{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl}}{{adj./n. 智力的；知识分子}}{{Intellectual property is protected by law.}}
{{intelligence}}{{/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns}}{{n. 智力；情报}}{{Artificial intelligence is advancing rapidly.}}
{{intense}}{{/ɪnˈtens}}{{adj. 强烈的；紧张的}}{{The competition was intense.}}
{{interfere}}{{/ˌɪntəˈfɪər}}{{v. 干涉；妨碍}}{{Please do not interfere with my work.}}
{{internal}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːnl}}{{adj. 内部的；国内的}}{{The company resolved its internal conflicts.}}
{{interpret}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt}}{{v. 解释；口译}}{{Different people may interpret the poem differently.}}
{{investigate}}{{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 调查；研究}}{{The police are investigating the cause of the fire.}}
{{involve}}{{/ɪnˈvɒlv}}{{v. 涉及；包含；使参与}}{{The project involves a lot of teamwork.}}
{{isolate}}{{/ˈaɪsəleɪt}}{{v. 隔离；孤立}}{{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of disease.}}
{{justify}}{{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ}}{{v. 证明…正当；为…辩护}}{{How can you justify spending so much money?}}
{{launch}}{{/lɔːntʃ}}{{v./n. 发射；启动；推出}}{{The company launched a new smartphone last week.}}
{{liberal}}{{/ˈlɪbərəl}}{{adj. 自由的；开明的}}{{She holds liberal views on social issues.}}
{{magnificent}}{{/mæɡˈnɪfɪsnt}}{{adj. 壮丽的；宏伟的}}{{The palace was a magnificent example of architecture.}}
{{manipulate}}{{/məˈnɪpjuleɪt}}{{v. 操纵；操作}}{{The company was accused of manipulating stock prices.}}
{{manufacture}}{{/ˌmænjuˈfæktʃər}}{{v./n. 制造；生产}}{{The factory manufactures electronic components.}}
{{margin}}{{/ˈmɑːdʒɪn}}{{n. 边缘；利润；余地}}{{The company operates on a narrow margin.}}
{{mechanism}}{{/ˈmekənɪzəm}}{{n. 机制；机械装置}}{{The clock has a complex mechanism.}}
{{mental}}{{/ˈmentl}}{{adj. 精神的；心理的}}{{Mental health is as important as physical health.}}
{{migrate}}{{/maɪˈɡreɪt}}{{v. 迁移；移居}}{{Many birds migrate south in winter.}}
{{military}}{{/ˈmɪlɪtəri}}{{adj./n. 军事的；军队}}{{The country increased its military spending.}}
{{moderate}}{{/ˈmɒdərət}}{{adj./v. 适度的；缓和}}{{Moderate exercise is beneficial to health.}}
{{modify}}{{/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ}}{{v. 修改；改变}}{{We need to modify the plan to fit the new requirements.}}
{{monitor}}{{/ˈmɒnɪtər}}{{n./v. 监视器；监控}}{{Doctors monitor the patient's condition closely.}}
{{motivate}}{{/ˈməʊtɪveɪt}}{{v. 激励；激发}}{{Good teachers motivate students to learn.}}
{{mutual}}{{/ˈmjuːtʃuəl}}{{adj. 相互的；共同的}}{{They have a mutual respect for each other.}}
{{negotiate}}{{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt}}{{v. 谈判；协商}}{{The two sides negotiated a peace agreement.}}
{{neutral}}{{/ˈnjuːtrəl}}{{adj. 中立的；中性的}}{{Switzerland remained neutral during the war.}}
{{norm}}{{/nɔːm}}{{n. 标准；规范}}{{Working from home has become the new norm.}}
{{notion}}{{/ˈnəʊʃn}}{{n. 概念；想法；意图}}{{The notion of equality is central to democracy.}}
{{objective}}{{/əbˈdʒektɪv}}{{n./adj. 目标；客观的}}{{The main objective of the project is to reduce costs.}}
{{obligation}}{{/ˌɒblɪˈɡeɪʃn}}{{n. 义务；责任}}{{Paying taxes is an obligation of every citizen.}}
{{occupy}}{{/ˈɒkjupaɪ}}{{v. 占据；使忙碌}}{{The meeting occupied the entire morning.}}
{{opponent}}{{/əˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 对手；反对者}}{{He defeated his opponent in the final match.}}
{{oppose}}{{/əˈpəʊz}}{{v. 反对；对抗}}{{Many citizens opposed the construction of the factory.}}
{{optimistic}}{{/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk}}{{adj. 乐观的}}{{She is optimistic about the future of the company.}}
{{outcome}}{{/ˈaʊtkʌm}}{{n. 结果；后果}}{{The outcome of the election surprised everyone.}}
{{outline}}{{/ˈaʊtlaɪn}}{{n./v. 轮廓；概述}}{{She outlined the main points of the plan.}}
{{outstanding}}{{/aʊtˈstændɪŋ}}{{adj. 杰出的；未解决的}}{{She is an outstanding scientist in her field.}}
{{overcome}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈkʌm}}{{v. 克服；战胜}}{{She overcame many difficulties to achieve her goal.}}
{{overseas}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈsiːz}}{{adv./adj. 海外的；在海外}}{{Many students choose to study overseas.}}
{{participate}}{{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 参加；参与}}{{All students are encouraged to participate in sports.}}
{{pattern}}{{/ˈpætn}}{{n. 模式；图案}}{{The pattern of behavior is hard to change.}}
{{perceive}}{{/pəˈsiːv}}{{v. 察觉；理解；认为}}{{She perceived a change in his attitude.}}
{{percentage}}{{/pəˈsentɪdʒ}}{{n. 百分比；比例}}{{A large percentage of the population lives in cities.}}
{{perform}}{{/pəˈfɔːm}}{{v. 执行；表演；表现}}{{The students performed well in the exam.}}
{{permanent}}{{/ˈpɜːmənənt}}{{adj. 永久的；持久的}}{{She found a permanent job in the city.}}
